# GROUP_ID review

> Only combination-level operating evidence is recorded here. A single course's mastery and stopping point
> still belong to that course's `progress.md`.
> A planned group keeps this file but writes no completion record; once it turns active, entries are
> appended per cycle.

## Cycle record template

```markdown
### Cycle N (closing day: YYYY-MM-DD)
1. Frequency red line: each member's actual count (met?)
2. Time deviation: budget Xh this cycle, actual Xh, one line on why
3. Days that failed to start: X days (which day, stuck at which entry point)
4. Members feeding each other: yes / no; evidence
5. This cycle's adjustment: at most one runtime parameter changed each time
```

## Group-level evaluation

The written examination runs per `main/50_playbook/exam_protocol.md`.

| Dimension | Major-adjustment window record | End of term |
|---|---|---|
| each member's capacity-goal attainment rate | | |
| frequency red-line compliance rate | | |
| total time-budget deviation | | |
| total days that failed to start | | |
| clearance rate of parked questions | | |
| debt handling: settled / carried over / waived by the user | | |
| recommendation for the next course group | | |

## Closing evidence

- [ ] exit retest evidence for every course member
- [ ] delivery or assessment evidence for every non-course member
- [ ] every debt has an explicit disposition
- [ ] the user has explicitly confirmed closing this group and starting the next
